    "source": "https://build.protomaps.com/20261111.pmtiles",
    "note": "Fourteen occupied PMTiles footprints establish the Water Training School courts, the long gallery, the waterfront pavilions and northern court ranges. Exterior photographs guide the grey tiled school façades, timber screens, light door and stone paving. Individual heights, courtyard paving alignments and the functions of unlabelled ranges are reconstructed. The native shoreline, ponds and public paths are retained. Outer landscape structures and the stele await identification. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
  },
  "review": "The three ranges retain their PMTiles footprints. The south-range veranda faces the paved approach visible in two aerial image versions. The short model walk follows sampled terrain outside the mapped building footprints, water and paths. A separate gate trial straddles this approach. The tea-house attribution and exact gate setback remain provisional. A failed load restores all 14 mapped footprints.",
